1
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:52,960
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:55,650
[Episode 10]

3
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:11,610
You're back.

4
00:01:15,039 --> 00:01:15,950
I'll get you a basin of water to wash—

5
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:19,260
♪ In March ♪

6
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,180
What the hell is this?

7
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:56,640
Take it away!

8
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:00,190
What is it?

9
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,500
What?

10
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,090
Take it away now!

11
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:34,300
Didn't you say

12
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:36,570
it was to treat your own illness?

13
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:37,800
How come—

14
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,190
He is my illness.

15
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:43,480
Once he's dead, I'll be cured.

16
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:48,430
It's all your fault.

17
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:50,120
If you hadn't pulled out the fangs,

18
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,020
it would have worked.

19
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,460
How can you blame me?

20
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:53,460
How was I supposed to know...

21
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:55,060
you wanted to do this?

22
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,990
One of us

23
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:06,520
has to die.

24
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,680
I don't want to die.

25
00:03:09,970 --> 00:03:11,430
Help me think of another way.

26
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,150
What?

27
00:03:14,250 --> 00:03:15,510
No way. I'm going to take a piss.

28
00:03:15,870 --> 00:03:16,740
Hey, what are you doing?

29
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,230
What are you doing? I-I-I...

30
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:19,910
If you help me kill him,

31
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:20,870
I'll marry you.

32
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:21,530
No, no, no.

33
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:22,579
That's really not necessary. Really.

34
00:03:22,579 --> 00:03:23,690
Mrs. Li, I'm begging you.

35
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:24,840
I really can't do this.

36
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,130
You've already done it once.

37
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:28,280
-When did I—
-You bought the snake.

38
00:03:29,329 --> 00:03:31,030
If Li Dewu goes to the police,

39
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,430
do you think they won't
find out you bought the snake?

40
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,590
You wouldn't get away with it anyway.

41
00:03:39,890 --> 00:03:41,750
Right now he's too scared
to think straight.

42
00:03:42,579 --> 00:03:43,930
Once he figures it out,

43
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,060
he'll know exactly who did it.

44
00:03:46,510 --> 00:03:48,180
He's so ruthless.

45
00:03:48,650 --> 00:03:51,070
I can't take his beatings.

46
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,320
The moment I'm in pain,

47
00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:53,390
I'll confess everything.

48
00:03:55,090 --> 00:03:56,800
Even if we leave aside the snake thing,

49
00:03:57,530 --> 00:03:59,020
just the fact that you slept with me

50
00:03:59,829 --> 00:04:01,480
would kill us both.

51
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:09,560
So,

52
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:12,580
you must help me get this done.

53
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:34,960
What's wrong, Mr. Li?

54
00:04:36,890 --> 00:04:38,640
You did it, didn't you?

55
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,909
What? What did I do?

56
00:04:42,070 --> 00:04:43,990
You lured the snake, didn't you?

57
00:04:44,930 --> 00:04:46,630
No, Mr. Li, stop joking.

58
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:48,770
H-How was I able

59
00:04:48,810 --> 00:04:49,770
to lure that thing?

60
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:51,000
Besides, I've been scared of that thing
since I was a kid.

61
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,130
Why would I lure it?

62
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,900
The Great Immortal said

63
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:56,070
snakes hibernate in winter.

64
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:59,050
To lure snake immortals out
in such cold weather,

65
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,830
the place has to be dry and hot.

66
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,510
So I was wondering,

67
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,650
where is dry and hot in my house?

68
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:10,580
Well...

69
00:05:10,610 --> 00:05:11,610
Your heating, of course.

70
00:05:11,630 --> 00:05:12,750
Your heating is so hot.

71
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:13,270
Wrong.

72
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,250
It's the woman's fire of jealousy!

73
00:05:16,390 --> 00:05:18,420
Did you tell her about

74
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:19,310
the hair salon?

75
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:20,180
Mr. Li, am I crazy?

76
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:22,070
Why would I tell her that?

77
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,300
I would never say that.

78
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:26,160
She stays home with the kid every day,

79
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:27,690
never stepping out of the house.

80
00:05:27,690 --> 00:05:28,680
You're the one who drives her around.

81
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,130
If you didn't tell her, who did?

82
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:31,540
Wait, Mr. Li.

83
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,870
Let me be honest with you.

84
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:34,500
I never gossip about you with Mrs. Li.

85
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,070
Really.

86
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,010
-Then what do you two talk about?
-Mr. Li.

87
00:05:37,010 --> 00:05:38,159
-What do you talk about?
-I'm driving.

88
00:05:38,159 --> 00:05:38,980
I'm turning. Turning.

89
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:50,350
Mr. Li, Mrs. Li and I—

90
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,570
we just don't have anything to talk about.

91
00:05:52,570 --> 00:05:53,130
We...

92
00:05:53,450 --> 00:05:55,810
never chat, really.

93
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,000
Let me tell you,

94
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:01,810
if the Shasha Hair Salon thing gets out,

95
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:03,570
I'll have someone kill you first.

96
00:06:03,570 --> 00:06:04,560
No, I—

97
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,190
Mr. Li, why would I
say anything about that?

98
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:07,000
Right?

99
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,630
Besides, I've worked for you for so long.

100
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:09,390
Got it?

101
00:06:10,010 --> 00:06:10,920
Got it.

102
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,370
I won't say a word. Don't worry.

103
00:06:22,830 --> 00:06:24,160
You have no idea.

104
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,320
That woman lately—

105
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:30,120
she's such a pain.

106
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:32,950
She's watching me like a hawk.

107
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,590
She's hit that age.

108
00:06:36,909 --> 00:06:38,909
Can't live without a man.

109
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:43,240
I don't have time
to deal with her every day.

110
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:46,480
I still have to beat her,

111
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:48,340
beat her to death!

112
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:51,190
Bitch.

113
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:21,680
If you don't kill him,

114
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,230
I can't live another day.

115
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:41,420
Hong.

116
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:44,220
Let's think it over.

117
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,300
Besides that,

118
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:48,190
is there no other way?

119
00:07:48,810 --> 00:07:49,659
There is.

120
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,010
What is it?

121
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:57,200
On a dark and windy night,

122
00:07:58,150 --> 00:08:00,010
you sneak over here,

123
00:08:00,370 --> 00:08:01,810
wearing red underpants,

124
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:03,600
and I'll wear a red dress.

125
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,330
One of us in the front yard,
the other in the back,

126
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:06,770
we'll hang ourselves on the doorframes,

127
00:08:06,770 --> 00:08:08,430
turning the Li family's house
into a haunted one.

128
00:08:08,450 --> 00:08:09,710
What do you think of this plan?

129
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:19,690
Wait, Hong.

130
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:21,480
Listen to me.

131
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:22,550
Listen.

132
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,740
Your plan is too dark.

133
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,500
We definitely won't
be reincarnated next life.

134
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:30,720
Let's do something more normal.

135
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:41,600
How about you two get a divorce?

136
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:52,900
No, no.

137
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:54,630
Hong.

138
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:56,700
Hong.

139
00:08:57,410 --> 00:08:58,030
Hong.

140
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,410
I was wrong.

141
00:08:59,410 --> 00:09:00,640
I'll never say that again.

142
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,090
Hong.

143
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,010
Hong.

144
00:09:10,010 --> 00:09:11,860
Just consider me talking nonsense, okay?

145
00:09:17,650 --> 00:09:19,120
How long have you worked for him?

146
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:21,800
Don't you know
what kind of person Li Dewu is?

147
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,170
Do you think he'd agree to a divorce?

148
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:29,580
Well, the main thing is,

149
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,460
murder is illegal.

150
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:33,220
If... If we get caught,

151
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,790
we'll both have to pay with our lives.

152
00:09:34,810 --> 00:09:36,360
Then don't get caught.

153
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:42,580
What do you mean?

154
00:09:46,850 --> 00:09:50,620
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

155
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:58,460
Alright.

156
00:09:58,460 --> 00:09:59,320
Hand him over to me.

157
00:10:03,630 --> 00:10:04,050
Mr. Li.

158
00:10:04,790 --> 00:10:06,120
Come on.

159
00:10:06,390 --> 00:10:09,080
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

160
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,330
Why's the ground standing up?

161
00:10:09,550 --> 00:10:10,320
Alright.

162
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,270
It's fine.

163
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:12,130
-It's fine.
-Mr. Li.

164
00:10:12,130 --> 00:10:13,370
The ground is standing up.

165
00:10:13,370 --> 00:10:14,580
Yeah, i-it's standing up.

166
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:15,610
I'm fine.

167
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:17,100
I'm fine.

168
00:10:17,650 --> 00:10:20,820
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

169
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:23,550
Zhang just made me drink too much.

170
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,020
He wouldn't drink.

171
00:10:26,050 --> 00:10:26,690
Yeah.

172
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,810
He made me drink.

173
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:31,160
I'll deal with him.

174
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,760
Mr. Li, slow down.

175
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:39,260
What? What did you say, Mr. Li?

176
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,510
The factory?

177
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:43,220
It's freezing cold.

178
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:44,610
Let's not go to the factory.

179
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:46,150
Mrs. Li is still waiting at home.

180
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:52,910
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

181
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:50,960
You shouted so loudly.

182
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:53,000
Are you afraid people
won't know where you're going?

183
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:55,670
No, he was making a scene just now.

184
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:56,720
And so many people were watching.

185
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,480
I had to let them know

186
00:10:56,790 --> 00:11:00,230
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

187
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,530
that he insisted on going himself

188
00:10:58,530 --> 00:10:59,650
and I didn't take him there.

189
00:10:59,790 --> 00:11:01,360
Why didn't you use a megaphone
to tell everyone

190
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,450
that you're going to freeze him to death?

191
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,820
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

192
00:11:02,650 --> 00:11:03,680
You idiot.

193
00:11:03,770 --> 00:11:04,620
Drive!

194
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:42,050
What if he doesn't freeze to death?

195
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:44,710
Half a pig left outside for two hours

196
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,100
would freeze solid.

197
00:11:46,210 --> 00:11:48,190
You think Fatty Li is thicker than a pig?

198
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:50,700
Not long ago,

199
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,620
someone froze to death at Yuhong Square.

200
00:11:52,810 --> 00:11:54,840
The cigarette in his hand was still lit.

201
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:58,010
But the person was frozen stiff.

202
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:00,420
That was a flashlight
he was biting, right?

203
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,130
He's dead heavy.

204
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:32,790
He's heavier than a pig.

205
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,650
Close the window.

206
00:12:38,650 --> 00:12:39,290
Let him lie down.

207
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:48,200
Help me close the window.

208
00:12:52,890 --> 00:12:54,630
The window is closed.

209
00:12:55,030 --> 00:12:56,790
Sleep tight.

210
00:13:10,850 --> 00:13:11,590
No, no.

211
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:13,230
It doesn't make sense.

212
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:14,870
Why would he come here
alone to sleep at night?

213
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:16,060
What do we say if the police ask?

214
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,530
What doesn't make sense?

215
00:13:17,530 --> 00:13:19,500
His old man Li Bin ruined this factory.

216
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,890
He's been playing here since he was a kid.

217
00:13:20,890 --> 00:13:21,980
He got drunk and wandered over.

218
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:22,750
Let's go.

219
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:23,700
Hurry.

220
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:25,040
[Dragon Palace Seafood Restaurant]

221
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:37,790
What? What did you say, Mr. Li?

222
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:40,470
T-The old factory?

223
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:41,390
It's freezing cold.

224
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:42,870
Let's not go to the old factory.

225
00:14:42,870 --> 00:14:44,330
Mrs. Li is still waiting at home.

226
00:15:03,510 --> 00:15:05,220
He didn't come back all night.

227
00:15:05,670 --> 00:15:07,200
I was worried sick.

228
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,480
He came back,

229
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,370
then went out again
in the middle of the night.

230
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:21,550
I don't even know where he went.

231
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:25,510
Maybe he's in some woman's bed.

232
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:28,970
He never tells me anything he does anyway.

233
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,650
It's not the first time
he's stayed out all night.

234
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:33,600
He's dead, isn't he?

235
00:16:22,510 --> 00:16:24,390
Are you trying to get me killed?

236
00:16:24,390 --> 00:16:25,290
No.

237
00:16:26,470 --> 00:16:27,740
So many people saw me

238
00:16:27,740 --> 00:16:29,100
pick up Boss Wu.

239
00:16:29,150 --> 00:16:30,030
If something really happened to him,

240
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,750
the first person
the cops come to would be me.

241
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:32,750
What the hell are you scared of?

242
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:33,590
I'll testify for you.

243
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:35,240
We agreed you wouldn't get involved.

244
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:36,890
Mrs. Li, I'm begging you.

245
00:16:36,890 --> 00:16:37,980
I'm begging you.

246
00:16:38,390 --> 00:16:39,730
Boss Wu really can't die.

247
00:16:39,770 --> 00:16:41,290
If he dies,
what am I supposed to say? I...

248
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,200
I won't be able to explain it.

249
00:16:56,010 --> 00:16:57,280
Did he notice anything?

250
00:16:58,460 --> 00:16:59,700
No, absolutely not.

251
00:17:00,270 --> 00:17:01,440
He slept like a log the whole way.

252
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:02,510
He almost froze to death.

253
00:17:02,510 --> 00:17:03,720
What could he notice?

254
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:05,230
He didn't say anything?

255
00:17:08,829 --> 00:17:09,750
He said one thing.

256
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:10,400
What did he say?

257
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:11,579
Close the window.

258
00:17:34,250 --> 00:17:35,050
You're up.

259
00:17:47,470 --> 00:17:48,970
Here, it's hot.

260
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:25,540
Look at what happened to my hand.

261
00:18:39,350 --> 00:18:40,790
I'll kick you to death.

262
00:18:40,790 --> 00:18:41,200
I—

263
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,240
You always open the window when you sleep.

264
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,640
Are you a penguin or what?

265
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:56,150
If you're a penguin,
go live in Antarctica!
